 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot A)$ where $N$ is the number of surfels and $A$ is the average area of a splat in pixels. Two passes double the rasterization cost compared to a single pass.
--   **Memory Complexity:** $O(W \cdot H)$ for the depth buffer, where $W$ and $H$ are screen dimensions.
--   **Performance:** Avoids the expensive view-dependent sorting required for correct alpha blending in a single pass [S1, unofficial]. However, it increases fragment overdraw due to the enlarged splats in Pass 2, which can impact pixel fillrate at close distances [S1, unofficial].
--   **Strengths:** Eliminates sharp square-shaped boundary artifacts; smooth appearance; hardware-friendly (no sorting).
--   **Limitations:** Only suitable for hermetic surfaces; not robust for fast-moving objects with large gaps; increased overdraw.
