 ## Background
-The method was proposed in the context of rendering scanned 4D media (3D geometry + time) using hardware-accelerated geometry instancing [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the limitations of standard surfel splatting, which suffers from artifacts due to alpha blending and rendering order. The two-pass approach was previously cited in literature [4, 5] (not provided in sources) as a viable alternative to sorting.
